From b472445322598c64b2c6197daf202ea68f1fad65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 22:05:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06935/11362] [outer-loop] flip SUBMITTED_AUTO_HUD_MASK_ENABLED
 on; defer levels_gained to live telemetry

Operator directive: after two offline matched-budget A/Bs (exp5584, exp5585)
both confirmed the mechanism's direct effect (distinct_states_delta: large,
consistent, HUD-positive-only reductions; positive control clean both
times; zero measured harm on the in-roster HUD-negative control game) but
both hit the same floor effect on levels_gained (no level-up reached in
EITHER arm on ANY roster game, at either the bare or the real submitted
search config) -- a limitation of the current from-scratch explorer's basic
capability ceiling on this roster, independent of auto_hud_mask -- the
operator rejected invoking the tier-3 LLM proposer to manufacture headroom
for a third offline A/B (the verified hidden-leaderboard top-3 all use NO
LLM proposer, per this session's comparative leaderboard analysis) and
instead deferred the levels_gained question to live-submission telemetry.

Deferring to live telemetry requires the mechanism to actually run during
live play for telemetry to exist to defer to, so SUBMITTED_AUTO_HUD_MASK_ENABLED
flips True on the strength of the established safety case (structurally the
mechanism can only collapse cells already proven action-invariant, never
introduce a false collapse of genuine board state), not a proven
levels_gained win. Updated REQ-ARC-WMTE-5583 with a full RESOLUTION record
and REQ-ARC-WMTE-5583-DEFAULT-PARITY (renamed from DEFAULT-OFF-PARITY) to
track the constant rather than assert a hardcoded value. Updated the two
test_arc_hud_mask.py assertions that hardcoded the old default to compare
against SUBMITTED_AUTO_HUD_MASK_ENABLED instead.

Verified zero new regressions: the same 53-file arc_competition_agent
regression sweep produces the identical 10 pre-existing failures / 335
passed as the pre-flip baseline (independently confirmed earlier this
session via an isolated worktree of the pre-change commit).

